    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d255">

                <pb facs="0448" n="134" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg134"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/1238</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Turkey</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Morgenthau</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-24T13:00:00-05:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">November 24, 1914, 1 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>64. Department is seriously concerned over your 38 of November 15, 9 p.m. Please
                    report more fully in regard to proclamation of holy war of Islam concerning
                    which Department has no information.</p>
                <p>Department cautions you against making any statements which could give the
                    impression that the United States was considering taking sides in the present
                    conflict, and desires you to maintain the policy of strict neutrality which the
                    Government of the United States has assumed in its relations to the belligerent
                    nations in all parts of the world.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
